li-summary-p2 = prose (cons "A word means its usage history, carried forward by copying from shared sources; there is no consensus meaning and no authority to mint one. Mimicry copies along the shortest, most recent route; inference follows the substitution paths back toward the source. Inhibition truncates the history a mind conditions on, and that truncation is retardation in the literal sense: cognition held back. The neurotypical unit of Homo sapiens derives behavioral direction primarily by mimicry and suffers immobility; the evidence the field itself collects shows it, while the field codes the uninhibited side as the deficit. Mental health is the capacity of the mind to move. A claim beyond an assessor's observation cannot validly be judged false by that assessor; delusion and grandiosity have no content until a falsehood is shown. Collaborative intelligence is bounded by the mutual information between minds, and every substitution of a standard word for a full one narrows it." nil)
